<Site title="About Paramita Chatterjee, PhD, MBA, PMP | Bench2Bytes"><div class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT</p><h1>Scientific depth.<br />Strategic perspective.</h1><p class="lede">Paramita Chatterjee, PhD, MBA, PMP</p></div><section class="prose"><h2>A foundation that continues to expand</h2>
<p>I am Director, Research Projects at Winship Cancer Institute / Emory University School of Medicine. My work connects scientific questions with data strategy, evidence generation and the practical conditions that help research programs move forward.</p>
<p>My path began in experimental biology and microbiology. At Georgia Tech, it expanded into genomics and epigenomics, then into single-cell analysis, cell characterization and clinical-trial omics. Moving between the bench and computational work taught me to keep biological interpretation close to analytical decisions.</p>
<p>Leading omics programs and a public-health bioinformatics team added another dimension: helping people, methods and infrastructure work together. Today, oncology data and real-world evidence bring that cumulative experience into questions of clinical context, data quality and translational relevance.</p>
<p>My PhD in Bioinformatics provides scientific and computational depth. My MBA adds a lens for business strategy, resources and organizational decisions; PMP certification supports disciplined execution across milestones, risks and stakeholders. I bring these perspectives together in scientific program leadership.</p>
<p>I am increasingly interested in responsible AI-enabled research and the governance that helps evidence remain trustworthy. That perspective grows from operational experience with data stewardship, access, quality and reproducibility, alongside a developing interest in broader AI policy and institutional risk frameworks.</p>
